    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (74.93) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier offensive engine; facing Davis Martin, his elite .478 xwOBA makes him the most dangerous bat in our lineup. Simultaneously, **Christian Yelich** benefits from a substantial platoon advantage against Tomoyuki Sugano. While Sugano carries a 5.12 xERA, the environment for **Christian Yelich** is optimized by an order-based boost, confirming his status as an elite start. In the middle tier, **Caleb Durbin** (67.91), **Trea Turner** (67.50), and **Lars Nootbaar** (67.19) provide reliable production, with **Trea Turner** particularly well-positioned to chase stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category\u2014against Will Warren.\n\nThe rotation decision for our outfield was heavily influenced by the projection for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (61.33). Despite Jared Jones presenting a tough matchup (3.25 xERA), **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s efficiency is buoyed by a significant dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and a high-leadoff-order expectation, keeping him ahead of the bench. The most difficult decision involved **Nelson Velazquez** (55.85), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Nelson Velazquez** projected well against the hittable Rhett Lowder, he was ultimately displaced by the superior efficiency scores of our starters. We are also monitoring **Casey Schmitt** (63.20), who carries a favorable wind-out projection in his matchup against Grayson Rodriguez, though this remains dependent on the final confirmation of his spot in the batting order.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that all lineups are currently pending. **Dillon Dingler** (40.31) is the most volatile asset in the lineup today; his score is suppressed by a negative platoon dynamic against Beck Way, placing him near our floor. We advise caution with **Dillon Dingler** and **Gary Sanchez** should their confirmed batting positions slide toward the bottom of the order, as their base projections offer little cushion. Overall, the Zebras are well-positioned, provided our high-speed threats like **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** maintain their top-of-order security throughout the day.",
